{#
  NOTE: this documentation is a Nunjucks comment, not an HTML one. It used
  to be a rendered <!-- --> block, which put ~3.5KB of prose into every page
  on the site — 16MB of it once /indicators/ started generating a page per
  indicator. Keep it as a Nunjucks comment so it stays in the source and out
  of the output. Nothing inside may contain a Nunjucks comment-close sequence,
  which would end this block early and spill the rest into every page.

  base.njk — Chollima Hunter base layout
    =======================================
    All other pages on the site MUST extend this layout via front matter:
  
        ---
        layout: base.njk
        title: "Page Title"
        ---
  
    EXTENSION POINTS (documented — do not rename without updating every
    downstream expert's templates):
  
    IMPORTANT — how this actually works: pages set `layout: base.njk` in
    front matter (as shown above) rather than using a Nunjucks {% extends %}
    tag, so Nunjucks never establishes a real extends/block-override chain
    here. Content injection instead relies on 11ty's own layout data cascade,
    which exposes the rendered page body as a `content` variable to the
    layout, and passes through any other front-matter/data keys the page
    defines (e.g. `extra_head`) the same way.
  
    (An earlier version of this file used {% block content %}{% endblock %}
    here, which silently rendered EMPTY on every page: with no {% extends %}
    in the child template, Nunjucks never overrides the layout's block, and a
    bare, never-overridden {% block %} in a standalone-rendered template just
    renders its own empty default. This broke every page's main content
    without causing a build error. Found and fixed by submission-intake
    during its build — see that expert's result notes for details.)
  
      content
        The main page body. Just write plain markup under your front matter
        in your own page template (see src/about/index.njk or
        src/submit/index.njk for examples). Rendered inside
        <main id="main-content"> via {{ content | safe }} below.
  
      extra_head
        Optional. Injects extra <head> content (e.g. a page-specific
        stylesheet link, extra meta tags). Set it as a plain front-matter key
        on your page, e.g.:
  
          ---
          layout: base.njk
          title: "Page Title"
          extra_head: "<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/assets/css/my-page.css\">"
          ---
  
        Rendered via {{ extra_head | safe }} just before </head> below. Leave
        it unset if you don't need it.

      noindex
        Optional. Set `noindex: true` in front matter to emit a robots
        noindex meta tag, as the 404 page does.
  
    NAV PATTERN:
      Nav items are data-driven from src/_data/nav.json, an array of
      { "label": string, "url": string } objects, looped with
      {% for item in nav %}. To add a nav item, edit nav.json — do NOT hardcode
      additional <li> elements in this file. All 6 non-home routes that other
      experts populate (Remote Workers, DPRK Hunting, Repo Scanner,
      EtherHiding, Sources, Submit IOCs) are already listed there, so nothing
      here needs to change when those experts run.
  
    BRAND MARK / SVG MOTIFS:
      The header brand mark is the Chollima pegasus raster asset (transparent) at
      src/assets/img/logo-mark.webp, rendered as an <img class="site-brand__mark">
      and sized by tokens.css. It is decorative — the surrounding <a> already
      carries the accessible name — so its alt is intentionally empty.
  
      A reusable inline SVG partial lives at src/_includes/svg/star.njk.
      Include it anywhere with:
        {% include "svg/star.njk" %}
      It is fully self-contained (no external image/CDN references).
  
    DESIGN TOKENS:
      CSS custom properties (palette, spacing, typography) are defined in
      src/assets/css/tokens.css, passed through untouched by 11ty and linked
      below. Reusable utility classes defined there include:
        .disclaimer-banner  — sourcing/attribution disclaimer banner
        .query-block        — copy-paste-able code/query block
#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  {#- Every script, style, font and image on the site is served from the site
      itself, and nothing is inline, so the policy can say exactly that. It is
      defence in depth for a site that renders scraped text: markup that slipped
      through escaping still could not load a script. GitHub Pages sets no
      response headers, hence a meta tag; frame-ancestors cannot be set here. #}
  <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'">
  {#- Outbound links already carry rel="noreferrer"; this covers everything
      else that leaves the site, such as an image or feed request. #}
  <meta name="referrer" content="strict-origin-when-cross-origin">
  {#- The home page leads with the site name and what it is, rather than the
      word "Home", since that title is what a search result shows. A page can
      set `head_title` to give the result a longer title than its heading and
      breadcrumb carry; an indicator page does, so the title names what kind
      of value it is as well as the value. #}
  {%- set pageTitle = "Chollima Hunter — DPRK cyber threat-intelligence tracker" if page.url == "/" else (head_title or title) + " — Chollima Hunter" %}
  <title>{{ pageTitle }}</title>
  <meta name="description" content="{{ description | default('Tracking, documenting, and exposing DPRK state-sponsored cyber campaigns, actors, and infrastructure.') }}">
  {%- if noindex %}
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
  {%- endif %}
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="Chollima Hunter">
  <meta property="og:title" content="{{ pageTitle }}">
  <meta property="og:description" content="{{ description | default('Tracking, documenting, and exposing DPRK state-sponsored cyber campaigns, actors, and infrastructure.') }}">
  <meta property="og:url" content="{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}">
  <meta property="og:image" content="{{ site.url }}/assets/img/icon-512.png">
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary">
  <meta name="twitter:title" content="{{ pageTitle }}">
  <meta name="twitter:description" content="{{ description | default('Tracking, documenting, and exposing DPRK state-sponsored cyber campaigns, actors, and infrastructure.') }}">
  <link rel="alternate" type="application/atom+xml" title="Chollima Hunter updates" href="/feed.xml">
  <link rel="icon" href="/assets/img/favicon.ico" sizes="any">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/assets/img/favicon-32.png">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="/assets/img/favicon-16.png">
  <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/assets/img/apple-touch-icon.png">
  <link rel="manifest" href="/site.webmanifest">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#0A0A0F">
  {#- Google Search Console ownership token for the chollimahunter@gmail.com
      property; the sitemap is submitted there. Removing it drops verification. #}
  <meta name="google-site-verification" content="BufHXHMNW6G5aUeRkSAhEBqnuohm5WVG-JFfMtzXbyE">
  {#- GitHub Pages sets no Cache-Control the site can tune, so the scripts that
      fetch the indicator indexes append this as a query string: a rebuild
      changes it, and a returning reader gets the new data instead of whatever
      their browser cached last month. #}
  <meta name="ioc-index-version" content="{{ iocIndex.generated_at }}">
  {#- The three faces every page paints first: body copy, the heading and the
      nav. Preloading them starts the fetch before the stylesheet is parsed,
      which is what turns the swap from fallback text into a flash instead of
      a visible reflow. The other weights load on demand as before. #}
  <link rel="preload" href="/assets/fonts/inter-400.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preload" href="/assets/fonts/space-grotesk-700.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preload" href="/assets/fonts/jetbrains-mono-500.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/tokens.css">
  {#- JSON-LD: breadcrumbs on every page, the site and organisation on the
      home page. A data block is not executed, so the CSP above does not
      apply to it. See partials/structured-data.njk. #}
  {% include "partials/structured-data.njk" %}
  {#- The site-wide scripts, loaded from the layout rather than per page
      because the elements they enhance sit in a dozen layouts and partials;
      each does nothing on a page without its element. site-utils.js holds
      the helpers the others call, so it loads first. table-sort.js makes
      every table with a header row sort by column on a click. #}
  <script src="/assets/js/site-utils.js" defer></script>
  <script src="/assets/js/table-sort.js" defer></script>
  <script src="/assets/js/table-stack.js" defer></script>
  <script src="/assets/js/result-tools.js" defer></script>
  <script src="/assets/js/filter-dropdown.js" defer></script>
  {{ extra_head | safe }}
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to main content</a>

  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="site-header__inner">
      <a class="site-brand" href="/" aria-label="Chollima Hunter home">
        <img class="site-brand__mark" src="/assets/img/logo-mark.webp" alt="" width="136" height="128" decoding="async">
        <span class="site-brand__names">
          <span class="site-brand__text">Chollima Hunter</span>
          {# The Korean is set one character per span so it can be spread
             edge to edge under the English name whatever Hangul font the
             reader's system falls back to; the whole name is read once, from
             the visually hidden copy. #}
          <span class="site-brand__ko" lang="ko">{% include "partials/ko-spread.njk" %}</span>
        </span>
      </a>

      <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Primary">
        <ul class="site-nav__list">
          {% for item in nav %}
          <li>
            <a href="{{ item.url }}" class="site-nav__link"{% if page.url == item.url %} aria-current="page"{% elif item.url != "/" and page.url and page.url.startsWith(item.url) %} aria-current="true"{% endif %}>{{ item.label }}</a>
          </li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="main-content" class="site-main" tabindex="-1">
    {{ content | safe }}
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <div class="site-footer__inner">
      <div class="site-footer__brand">
        {% set star_decorative = true %}{% include "svg/star.njk" %}
        <span>&copy; 2026 Chollima Hunter — a public DPRK cyber threat-intelligence tracker.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="site-footer__links">
        <a href="/about/">About and policies</a>
        <a href="/guidance/">If you find a match</a>
        <a href="/data/">Data and downloads</a>
        <a href="/glossary/">Glossary</a>
        {%- if site.repoUrl %}
        <a href="{{ site.repoUrl }}" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source on GitHub</a>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if site.businessEmail and "TODO" not in site.businessEmail %}
        <a href="mailto:{{ site.businessEmail }}">Contact</a>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if site.kofiUrl %}
        <a class="donate-button" href="{{ site.kofiUrl }}" rel="noopener noreferrer">Support this project</a>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
